The include/ headers are unchanged ds41 W1 attention sources from
chronarion/dsv41 commit f8cd311caf3328ed6f4bb158a7c12811e32a06f8:
https://github.com/chronarion/dsv41/tree/f8cd311caf3328ed6f4bb158a7c12811e32a06f8/kernels/vendor/ds41/w1-attn

The upstream vendor identifies Garner McCloud's dgx-station-recipes,
deepseek-v4.1-flash recipe, commit 8043a68, as its source. LICENSE.ds41 and
NOTICE.upstream retain its license and attribution. These are the fused
SM103 decode-attention kernels selected by DerpSeek's exact profile.

Flare's Python binding builds the extension during model preparation against
the installed Torch ABI. csrc/w1_attn.cu carries the upstream launcher with an
added thread-safe set_num_sms(int) / get_num_sms() override of num_sms() so
cooperative launches clamp their CTA grid to a CUDA Green Context compute
partition; the device kernels in include/ are unchanged.
